  "id": "COMPOUND:21930 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Ancistrobenomine A is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol. These compounds are all known to interact with the replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential mechanism where Ancistrobenomine A may exert its effect through a shared pathway involving Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence points to a possible dependency on the demethylase activity for the replication of the replicase polyprotein 1ab, with Ancistrobenomine A acting as a modulator in this process. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Ancistrobenomine A in targeting the replicase polyprotein 1ab via a mechanism involving demethylase inhibition, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
